<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dipayal Silgadhi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dipayal Silgadhi is a town in Doti district in far-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, on the Seti River. Dipayal was a seat of the Raika kings of Doti, and Silgadhi, the old town on the ridge above, was the trading centre of the region. Until 2015 the town was the headquarters of Nepal's Far-Western Development Region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dipayal-silgadhi.jpg" alt="Dipayal Silgadhi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bhaskar Pyakurel · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dipayal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
